   "evidence": "Identical terms at Center/IdentityComponent.lean:56-58 and Center/Finite.lean:54-56. Mathlib has no such instance: grep for `IsReduced.*\u29f8 nilradical` / `isReduced_quotient` in ./mathlib returns no matches; `TauCeti.HopfIdeal.isReduced_quotient_reduction` (Algebra/AlgebraicGroup/HopfIdeal/Reduction.lean:40) is a theorem about `CommHopfAlgCat.quotient`, not this instance, and `Center/Reduced.lean` exposes only the theorem `isReduced_reducedCenterCoordinateHopfAlgebra`, so nothing downstream can synthesize it.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/AlgebraicGroup/Center/IdentityComponent.lean",
   "fix": "State it once and publicly: `instance {R : Type*} [CommRing R] : IsReduced (R \u29f8 nilradical R)` in a canonical commutative-algebra module (e.g. `TauCeti/RingTheory/Ideal/Nilpotent.lean`), import it here, and delete both `local instance` copies (this one and `TauCeti/Algebra/AlgebraicGroup/Center/Finite.lean:54`).",
   "issue": "`local instance : IsReduced ((centerCoordinateHopfAlgebra H) \u29f8 nilradical ...)` is a specialization of the fully general fact `IsReduced (R \u29f8 nilradical R)`, whose proof `(Ideal.isRadical_iff_quotient_reduced _).mp (Ideal.radical_isRadical \u22a5)` does not depend on this file's subject. Keeping it `local` means the file's public statements (e.g. `reducedCenterIdentityComponentDefiningIdeal_def`, which mentions `reducedCenterCoordinateHopfAlgebra H`) cannot be restated downstream under `[IsAlgClosed k] [Algebra.FiniteType k H]` without re-proving the instance; Center/Finite.lean:54 already had to do exactly that, and this PR makes it two copies.",
   "line": "56"
  }
 ],
